codex
The HealthKit question is now definitive: `workout-processing` is a watchOS-only background mode. Apple’s Xcode documentation describes it as tracking activity “on Apple Watch,” and the WWDC25 iPhone workout session explicitly describes builder metrics as live “while your app is in the foreground.” On iPhone, the session lets HealthKit continue the workout/sensor collection and permits locked-device data access after consent; it does not grant your process watchOS-style continuous CPU time.

That means the current cap alarm has two unsupported dependencies: a silent-audio runtime hack and a callback from `HKLiveWorkoutBuilder` that is not promised after iOS suspends the app. An observer query plus background delivery is useful for eventual sample ingestion, but it is not a second-by-second alarm clock.
